course: dictionary
lesson: 12839
title: Encircled: surrounded all the way round
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When something is encircled, it has been surrounded, so there is a ring of things or people all the way around it. «The wolves encircled the camp» means the wolves formed a circle around the tents, so nobody could walk out. Look for the clue: the word circle is hidden inside encircled.
explain: Encircled is the past form of the verb encircle. The verb changes its ending: encircle, encircles, encircled, encircling. «The hedge encircles the garden» happens now, but «The hedge encircled the garden» tells you it happened in the past.
explain: You can also use encircled to describe a place. Long ago, an army could encircle a city, which means it surrounded the city so the people inside could not escape. Ask yourself: is there a ring of something around the thing? If yes, encircled probably fits.
fact: Encircled means formed a circle around something or someone, or surrounded it.
fact: «The wolves encircled the camp» creates danger, because the campers cannot run away.
fact: In war, an army that encircled a city surrounded it so the people inside could not escape.
fact: In maths or art, a shape can be encircled by a ring, such as a circle drawn around a number.
fact: Encircle has four forms: encircle, encircles, encircled and encircling.
exercise: «The hedge encircled the garden.» What does encircled mean? | *Surrounded all the way round | Jumped over | Painted green | Cut down and removed
exercise: «The army encircled the old town, so no one could leave.» What did the army do? | Built a bridge over the river | Sang a song | Ran away from the town | *Surrounded the town so it could not escape
exercise: «The star was encircled by a ring of red dots.» What does encircled mean? | Painted in blue | Hidden under the dots | Dropped on the floor | *Surrounded by a ring
test: «The children encircled the teacher to hear the story.» What does encircled mean? | Painted | Ignored | Ran away from | *Stood in a ring around
test: «The farmer's dog encircled the sheep and kept them together.» What did the dog do? | *Ran in a ring around the sheep | Slept under a tree | Ate the sheep | Ran away from the farm
exam: Which word means surrounded all the way round? | *Encircled | Glum | Famished | Barely
